    "updated_at": "2020-06-24T15:54:31Z",
    "body": "1. It seems this allows for reducing the effective scope of _storedResponse_. We should probably make the text reflect that.\r\n2. And yeah, I think we should have some tests here to be sure. I also would not expect implementations to do a lot of this properly. E.g., combining of headers is one of the areas with known bugs (and perhaps some lack of clarity in the protocol as to which headers can be updated and such; see https://github.com/httpwg/http-core/issues/165).",
